cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below, and cite the accompanying article."
type: software
title: "Code for: Body Mass Index: Mathematical Foundation of the World's Most Widely Used Adiposity Index in Pediatrics"
abstract: >-
  R pipeline that reproduces every figure, Table 2, every number quoted in the text, and the
  figure source data for a review of the mathematics of body mass index (BMI) in pediatrics.
  It downloads public NHANES 1999–2023 files and the CDC 2022 BMI-for-age reference, estimates
  age- and sex-specific weight–height allometric exponents, the height–body fat association,
  and the stability of body composition at fixed BMI across the life course (DXA, NHANES
  1999–2006 and 2011–2016).
